Provider marks in apps/dashboard/lib/provider-icons.ts come from Simple Icons
(https://simpleicons.org, CC0-1.0), version and slug per icon in that file's
header. The names and marks of Vercel, Cloudflare, Google (Firebase, Google
Cloud), GitHub, GitLab, Netlify, Render, Railway, Fly.io, DigitalOcean,
HashiCorp (Terraform), Amazon Web Services, Microsoft (Azure) and Heroku are
trademarks of their respective owners. infralift uses them only to identify the
service a connection is for, and is not affiliated with or endorsed by them.
The AWS, Azure and Heroku marks are plain initials drawn for infralift, not
those companies' logos.

Vendor API descriptions (apps/api/e2e/specs)

The e2e suite commits subsets of vendors' published API descriptions: only the
operations infralift calls and what they reference, extracted and modified by
apps/api/e2e/specs/extract.ts (examples removed; Swagger 2.0, Google discovery
documents and Heroku's hyper-schema converted to OpenAPI; GraphQL schemas cut
to the fields queried; seeded examples added). Each file carries its upstream
copyright and licence notice in info.license and info.x-infralift-notice (JSON)
or a comment header (GraphQL SDL). Each upstream LICENSE, copied verbatim at
the pinned commit, is in apps/api/e2e/specs/licenses/.

