Full commits and paths are in apps/api/e2e/specs/sources.ts. None of the
upstream repositories has a NOTICE file of its own, so Apache-2.0 section 4(d)
adds nothing beyond the licence text and this statement of modification.

tfc.openapi.json is a modified subset of a file under the Mozilla Public
License 2.0. A subset is a Modification (MPL 2.0, section 1.10), so the file
remains Covered Software under the MPL 2.0: it carries the MPL's Exhibit A
notice, the licence text is apps/api/e2e/specs/licenses/tfc.LICENSE, and its
Source Code Form is the file itself (it is distributed only as source). The
MPL is file-level, so it does not extend to the rest of infralift.

Render's API description (api-docs.render.com) is used but not committed: it
states no licence. scripts/e2e.sh fetches it at setup from an archived copy
pinned by sha256 and writes it to a git-ignored path.
